OBSERVED (by karr-worker during task #13, causing accidental writes to the
REAL dogfood board that had to be restored from dangling commits)

  karr --dir /some/other/repo list   # documented as overriding discovery
  => silently uses the board of the CURRENT directory instead

App/karr.pm documents: "The global --dir option overrides" board discovery,
and an option dir => (...) exists at the root command. But discovery
(BoardDiscovery role / Git->new(dir => ".")) never receives it — several Cmds
hardcode dir => "." (e.g. Cmd/Restore.pm:64).

IMPACT: high — a caller believing they target an isolated board mutates
whatever board the cwd belongs to, and sync_after pushes that to its remote.
Exactly this polluted the dogfood board during #13 (remediated).

FIX DIRECTION: thread the root dir option through to BoardDiscovery/Git in
all Cmds, or reject --dir loudly as unimplemented until it works.

Repo VERSION 0.304.
